**The Chactun dataset, and anything derived from it.**

    Kokalj, Z., Somrak, M., et al. (2023). Machine learning-ready remote
    sensing data for Maya archaeology. Scientific Data 10:558.
    https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02455-x
    Data: https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.22202395
    Licensed CC BY 4.0. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

CC BY 4.0 requires attribution and does NOT impose ShareAlike. This is the
material difference from the SpaceNet terms above, and it is what determines
what may be released:

  - Derived material -- converted COCO annotations, exported detections,
    rendered figures -- carries the attribution obligation and nothing more.
  - Trained model weights derived from this data MAY be released, provided
    Kokalj et al. 2023 is attributed. Contrast the SpaceNet weights below,
    which cannot be released without carrying ShareAlike.

The visualisation recipe used for the cross-survey transfer work -- sky-view
factor, positive openness and slope with the general-terrain stretch settings
-- is Table 3 of the same paper and is attributed there.

None of the derived material is tracked in this repository; it is regenerated
from the source data by the scripts.

**Third-party software.** detectron2, PyTorch, GDAL, rasterio, shapely and the
rest carry their own terms. See "Third-party components" in README.md.

**Trained model weights.** The two datasets differ here and the distinction
matters. Weights derived from SpaceNet 2 imagery are a derivative of CC BY-SA
material: they are not tracked here, and releasing them would carry the
ShareAlike obligation with them. Weights derived from the Chactun data are a
derivative of CC BY 4.0 material and may be released with attribution to
Kokalj et al. 2023; the Chactun detector is published on the Hugging Face Hub
on that basis. No weights of either kind are tracked in this repository.
